                <pb facs="1262" n="1166" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg1166"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Grip to Mr. Day.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Sweden and Norway</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-07-16"><hi rendition="#italic">July 16,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary of State</hi>: I have the honor to
                    acknowledge receipt of your excellency’s note of the 15th instant by which you
                    are pleased to inform me of the forms which the Government of the United States
                    desires to see observed by the neutral vessels of war which are destined for
                    blockaded ports in the island of Cuba and particularly for Habana.</p>
                <p>I shall not fail to advise my Government without delay of this important
                    communication.</p>
                <p>Be pleased to accept, etc.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">A. Grip.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
